Subject: [PATCH 0/3] ui/spice: make non-GL damage handling stream-friendly

RFC / prototype. The non-GL spice display unions all damage into one
box, slices it into 32 pixel columns, and only pushes it on the 30ms
refresh timer. With streaming-video=filter a guest playing a 480x360
video at 30 fps (virtio-vga, Linux guest) makes spice-server 0.15.2
start 18-19 separate 32x360 streams while ~4900-6700 small lossless
column draws keep flowing; over 28s the display channel carried
21-29 MB. With this series it is one 480x360 stream plus 45 draws,
6.7 MB. Damage-to-QXL-command latency (qemu trace) drops from
p50 15ms / p95 29ms to p50 1-2ms / p95 15ms with patch 3.

Patch 1: track up to 16 disjoint damage rects instead of one box.
Patch 2: diff only to trim/split each rect, send one DRAW_COPY per box.
Patch 3: push damage on a paced (16ms) timer instead of the refresh.

Not yet done: tests, a knob for the pacing interval (or reuse of
max-refresh-rate), measurement with VGA / Windows guests.

Michael Still (3):
  ui/spice: track a bounded list of damage rectangles
  ui/spice: send each damaged region as one DRAW_COPY
  ui/spice: push damage promptly instead of on the refresh timer

